/**
 * @file spl.dox
 * @brief SPL DSL overview.
 *
 * The project accepts a theory-aligned Boolean SPL DSL.
 *
 * Top-level sections:
 * - `SPL <name>`
 * - `FEATURES <count> <feature...>`
 * - optional `CONSTRAINTS ... ASSERT <formula> ... END`
 * - optional `AVAILABLE_SYSTEMS ... END`
 * - optional `MISSING_SYSTEMS ... END`
 * - optional `CATEGORY_FILTER ...`
 *
 * Formulas support Boolean connectives `!`, `&&`, `||`, `->`, `<->`, literals
 * `TRUE` and `FALSE`, and cardinality constraints such as
 * `COUNT(a, b, c) <= 2` and `COUNT(a, b, c) IN [1,2]`.
 *
 * `COUNT(...)` counts selected Boolean features. It is part of the paper-aligned
 * core and should not be confused with repeated-feature multiplicity, which is
 * outside the current DSL.
 *
 * The parser stores asserted formulas in `spl_specification_t::m_constraints`
 * as a theory-native AST (`theory_formula_t`). Valid systems are derived only
 * from those formulas. `CATEGORY_FILTER` is a post-classification reporting
 * filter and never changes the generated feature space.
 */
